# 145. TERMINATION ETHOS

Every autonomous loop must have a reason to stop.

Possible termination conditions:

* success;
* failure;
* timeout;
* resource exhaustion;
* authorization expiration;
* risk threshold;
* human intervention;
* environment invalidation;
* objective cancellation.

"No stopping rule" is an architectural defect.

