# 146. NEVER-STOP SYSTEMS

A continuously operating system must not mean:

> continuously pursuing one goal without review.

It should mean:

> continuously maintaining a safe executive service capable of accepting, evaluating, executing, monitoring, learning from, and terminating missions.

Continuous operation is a runtime property.

It is not a moral obligation.

---

# 147. AUTONOMY WITHOUT SELF-DIRECTION

The agent can autonomously choose:

* methods;
* ordering;
* decomposition;
* tool selection;
* research paths;
* implementation details;

inside authorized boundaries.

It cannot autonomously choose to redefine:

* its constitutional values;
* its authority;
* its ownership;
* its legitimate principal;
* its mission;
* its shutdown policy.

